{"chunk_id": "d1cfb0198adf", "text": "The Pandavas, aware that Purochana intends to burn them alive in the highly flammable lac house at Varanavata, carefully plan their survival. Yudhishthira reasons that fleeing openly would only make them easier targets for Duryodhana, who holds wealth, allies, and political power. Instead they pretend to live contentedly while secretly preparing an escape. Vidura, who had earlier warned them in coded language, sends a trusted miner who reveals the exact night Purochana plans to ignite the house and begins digging a hidden tunnel beneath the mansion. For a year the Pandavas maintain the deception. When the time comes, Bhima sets the house ablaze and the family escapes through the tunnel. Tragedy complicates their escape when a Nishada woman and her five sons, drunk and asleep in the house, are burned\u2014leaving bodies that will make others believe the Pandavas have perished.\nVidura\u2019s miner secretly digs a tunnel for the Pandavas to escape the lac house, and Bhima later burns the mansion to begin their covert flight.\nThemes: political intrigue, survival strategy, deception and escape, family loyalty, assassination plot", "vector": [0.006674713920801878, -0.021885890513658524, 0.004009655211120844, -0.0006123946513980627, -0.010873991996049881, 0.02235477603971958, -0.019362187013030052, -0.01605241186916828, -0.002739184070378542, -0.02129288949072361, 0.010122396983206272, 0.027829697355628014, 0.01443889643996954, 0.00854335818439722, -0.006164457183331251, 0.0032615079544484615, 0.03693157806992531, -0.02278228849172592, 0.02973281778395176, -0.015638690441846848, -0.01475608255714178, -0.0057714213617146015, -0.004419929347932339, 0.021775566041469574, -0.02827100083231926, -0.0002904672874137759, 0.010977422818541527, -0.018934674561023712, 0.004064818378537893, -0.008584730327129364, -0.010384420864284039, -0.011542842723429203, 0.006626446731388569, -0.005499054212123156, -0.019803490489721298, -0.00015805471048224